From 79803bd802932da3655dfd763f0e1c87bfe42824 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:26:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] WIP: fix(validator): assert the schema's `byte` format on
 the wire
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A `tools/call` result whose image `data` was `not base64!` passed the wire
schema and drew no finding at all: the specification's `schema.json` marks
image and audio `data` and resource `blob` with `format: byte`, and format
assertion was off. The wire-schema check now asserts `byte` with the base64
rule the resource and prompt checks already apply (RFC 4648 §4 alphabet,
groups of four, `=`/`==` padding, the empty string included); `uri` and
`uri-template` stay annotations as ADR-0020 decided. Both vendored schemas use
exactly those three formats. The official suite
(`@modelcontextprotocol/conformance@0.2.0-alpha.12`) loads `ajv-formats` and
then `addFormat("byte", true)`, so it asserts the two URI formats and never
`byte`: the engines disagree on exactly those three, in opposite directions.

Three corpus traces pin it (a 2025-11-25 and a 2026-07-28 tool result with a
non-base64 image, failing the wire schema and nothing else; a conforming
session with every padding length and an empty `data`), with goldens and
ledger rows; the three existing goldens whose traces carry `not base64!`
(prom-003, prom-004, res-006) now also fail the wire schema on the same
message. Unit tests under `wire_schema/tests/formats.rs` failed before the
change (3 of 4) and pass after.

WIP: the focused tests, `cargo xtask bless` and `cargo xtask coverage --check`
ran green; the full workspace test run was still in flight, and clippy, fmt,
doc, gates and the mutation runs for this change have not been run yet.

